course: dictionary
lesson: 10640
title: UNICEF and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: UNICEF is a proper noun. It is the name of one special organization, so it starts with a capital letter, and its letters are all capitals too. You can often work out what a name like this does from the words around it.
explain: «The UN has agencies for special tasks, such as UNICEF for children, the World Health Organization for health and the World Food Programme for hunger.» The context tells you that an agency is a group set up for a special job, and that UNICEF's job is children.
explain: UNICEF is part of the United Nations, and it works to help children around the world. The letters once stood for longer words, «United Nations International Children's Emergency Fund». Today it is called the United Nations Children's Fund, but the short name has stayed.
fact: A proper noun is the name of one particular person, place or organization, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: UNICEF is part of the United Nations and works to help children around the world, giving them food, clean water, vaccines, schooling and protection.
fact: The letters first stood for «United Nations International Children's Emergency Fund»; today the name is the United Nations Children's Fund, but the old letters are kept.
fact: «Support UNICEF» means help it, often by giving money, and schools do this on charity days.
fact: The Convention on the Rights of the Child (1989) is a key UNICEF topic in lessons on human rights.
exercise: «The UN has agencies for special tasks, such as UNICEF for children, the World Health Organization for health and the World Food Programme for hunger.» Which agency works for children? | World Food Programme | World Health Organization | *UNICEF
exercise: In «agencies for special tasks», what does agencies most likely mean? | *Groups set up to do a special job | Birds that fly very far | Long lists of names | Children's toys
exercise: UNICEF's old letters stood for longer words. Today the organization is called what? | Children's Toy Fund | *United Nations Children's Fund | World Health Organization | United Nations International Children's Emergency Fund
test: Why does UNICEF start with a capital letter? | Because it is a very important word | Because it is a long word | Because it is always written in bold | *Because it is the name of one special organization
test: What does UNICEF give children? | *Food, clean water, vaccines, schooling and protection | Sweets and toys only | Roads and bridges for cars | Weather forecasts for the week
exam: Schools raise money for UNICEF on charity days, so «support UNICEF» most likely means | Forget about it | *Help it, for example by giving money | Copy its name onto a poster | Argue with it
